fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-changing-duration',title:'A habit that ended',outcome:'I can say how long a former situation lasted and when it changed.',takeaway:'Per plus a bounded period commonly uses passato prossimo; imperfetto describes an old habit or background state before a change.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-then-now'],words:[['per tre anni','for three years'],['fino al 2020','until 2020'],['trasferirsi','to move home'],['abitare','to live']],models:[['Describe the old stretch','For a completed three-year period, use passato prossimo; reserve imperfetto for an old habit or background state.','Per tre anni ho abitato a Torino.','For three years I lived in Turin.'],['Mark the change','A completed move ends the old situation.','Nel 2020 mi sono trasferita a Firenze.','In 2020 I moved to Florence.']],checks:[['Per due anni ___ vicino alla scuola; poi mi sono trasferito.','For two years I lived near the school; then I moved.','ho abitato',['ho abitato','abiterò','abitavo'],'Per due anni is a completed bounded period here.','Use passato prossimo for the completed two-year stretch.'],['Fino al 2022, noi ___ ogni giorno in treno; poi abbiamo cambiato lavoro.','Until 2022, we travelled by train every day; then we changed jobs.','viaggiavamo',null,'The daily travel was a past routine.','Use the noi imperfetto of viaggiare.'],['Da bambina Lisa ___ in campagna; nel 2015 si è trasferita in città.','As a child Lisa lived in the countryside; in 2015 she moved to the city.','viveva',['viveva','ha vissuto','vivrà'],'The old state lasted before the dated change.','Choose the background form.'],['Per molti anni Paolo ___ nello stesso ufficio; l’anno scorso ha cambiato sede.','For many years Paolo worked in the same office; last year he changed location.','ha lavorato',null,'Per molti anni names a completed period before the change last year.','Use passato prossimo for the bounded stretch.']],application:['Explain a life change','Tell a new colleague where you used to live or work and what changed.','Per tre anni ho lavorato a Milano. L’anno scorso ho cambiato lavoro e mi sono trasferita a Bologna.',['The former period and dated change are distinguishable.','Imperfetto describes the old situation.','A completed form names the change.'],'speak']});

// B1.4: keep both recipient and object referents recoverable.
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-recipient-reference',title:'Keep the recipient clear',outcome:'I can use a recipient pronoun without losing track of who receives something.',takeaway:'Use mi, ti, gli, le, ci or vi only when the recipient is clear; repeat the name if needed.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-changing-duration'],words:[['la mail','email'],['mandare','to send'],['il collega / la collega','colleague'],['rispondere','to reply']],models:[['Name the recipient first','Introduce the person before replacing the name with a pronoun.','Ho scritto a Sara. Le ho mandato la mail.','I wrote to Sara. I sent her the email.'],['Change recipient carefully','Gli can refer to a male singular recipient; the context must identify him.','Ho chiamato Luca e gli ho spiegato il problema.','I called Luca and explained the problem to him.']],checks:[['Ho scritto a Sara e ___ ho mandato la foto.','I wrote to Sara and sent her the photo.','le',['le','gli','lo'],'Le points back to Sara as recipient.','Which indirect pronoun refers to Sara?'],['Ho parlato con Marco e ___ ho dato il numero.','I spoke with Marco and gave him the number.','gli',null,'Marco is the recipient; gli means to him.','Use the indirect pronoun for Marco.'],['Io e Luca abbiamo chiamato i colleghi; ___ abbiamo spiegato il piano.','Luca and I called the colleagues; we explained the plan to them.','gli',['gli','li','ci'],'Gli can refer to the colleagues as recipients in this context.','The colleagues receive the explanation.'],['Marta mi ha scritto; ___ ho risposto subito.','Marta wrote to me; I replied to her immediately.','le',null,'Rispondere takes an indirect recipient; le refers to Marta.','Do not use a direct object pronoun with rispondere.']],application:['Pass on a request','Write a short update saying whom you contacted and what you gave or explained to them.','Ho chiamato Sara. Le ho dato il numero del medico e le ho spiegato l’orario.',['Every pronoun has a clear named recipient.','The recipient pronoun fits the person.','The object or information remains explicit.']],passage:{title:'Passing on a message',it:'Ho chiamato Marta e le ho detto l’orario. Poi ho scritto a Luca e gli ho mandato l’indirizzo. Entrambi hanno risposto subito.',en:'I called Marta and told her the time. Then I wrote to Luca and sent him the address. Both replied at once.',mode:'listen',task:'Identify the recipient of each piece of information.'}});
oldLesson('B1','b1-double-pronouns','v2-b1-double-pronouns',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-recipient-reference'],facet:'recipient-plus-object',words:[['prestare','to lend'],['la chiave','key'],['restituire','to return'],['spiegare','to explain']],portfolio:{title:'Offer to send something',prompt:'Write a short message offering to send a named item to a named person, then refer to both with a combined pronoun.',model:'Ho la foto di Sara. Se vuoi, te la mando stasera.',rubric:['The recipient and object are introduced clearly.','The combined pronoun has the right order and gender/number.','The offer is natural for the relationship.']}});
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-pronoun-request',title:'Ask someone to pass it on',outcome:'I can use a combined pronoun in a request or answer.',takeaway:'In a finite polite request, a combined pronoun can stand before the verb; with an affirmative tu command, it attaches to the command.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-double-pronouns'],words:[['il modulo','form'],['la risposta','reply'],['passare','to pass'],['mandare','to send']],models:[['Use the pair before a finite verb','Me lo refers to an already known masculine object being sent or given to me.','Il modulo? Me lo puoi mandare?','The form? Can you send it to me?'],['Attach it to an affirmative command','In a familiar affirmative command, the pair attaches: mandamelo. Keep the recipient and object clear.','Il modulo? Mandamelo domani, per favore.','The form? Send it to me tomorrow, please.']],checks:[['Il modulo? ___ puoi mandare oggi?','The form? Can you send it to me today?','Me lo',['Me lo','Te la','Gli li'],'Me lo means the form to me.','Identify both the recipient and object.'],['La foto? ___ puoi mostrare?','The photo? Can you show it to me?','Me la',null,'La refers to foto; me is the recipient.','Use the feminine object in the pair.'],['Il biglietto? Per favore, ___ domani.','The ticket? Please send it to me tomorrow.','mandamelo',['mandamelo','mandamela','me manda'],'The masculine ticket is lo, attached after manda and me.','Use the affirmative tu command plus me lo.'],['Le chiavi? Per favore, ___ subito.','The keys? Please bring them to me at once.','portamele',null,'Le refers to feminine plural chiavi in the attached pair.','Attach me le to porta.']],application:['Get a document from a friend','Write two short turns: mention a specific item, request it with a pronoun, and give a plausible reply.','— Hai il modulo? Me lo puoi mandare?\n— Certo, te lo mando stasera.',['The item and recipient are identifiable.','The combined pronouns keep the correct order.','The request and reply fit the same item.'],'interact','Ask a partner for a different item; listen to which pronoun they use in the reply.']});

// B1.5: ci and ne are separately grounded before ce ne and agreement.
oldLesson('B1','b1-ci-place','v2-b1-ci-place',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-pronoun-request'],facet:'place-reference',words:[['la biblioteca','library'],['il bar','café or bar'],['tornare','to return'],['andarci','to go there']],passage:{title:'Back to the same place',it:'Ieri sono andata in biblioteca. Ci torno anche domani: lì riesco a studiare meglio. Dopo, vado al bar vicino e ci incontro Marta.',en:'Yesterday I went to the library. I am going back there tomorrow too: I can study better there. Afterwards, I go to the nearby café and meet Marta there.',mode:'listen',task:'Notice which earlier places ci refers to.'}});
oldLesson('B1','b1-ne-quantity','v2-b1-ne-quantity',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-ci-place'],facet:'quantity-or-di-reference',words:[['le arance','oranges'],['il biglietto','ticket'],['di quel problema','about that problem'],['due','two']],cards:[...allOld['b1-ne-quantity'].objectives[0].teach,{title:'Ce ne and past agreement',body:'Before a finite verb, ci becomes ce beside ne: Ce ne servono due. With a preceding ne and a stated quantity in compound past, the participle can agree with the item: Ne ho comprate tre (arance).',examples:[{it:'Ce ne servono due. Ne ho comprate tre.',en:'We need two of them. I bought three of them (feminine plural).'}]}],questions:revisedQuestions('b1-ne-quantity',{0:{context:'Vuoi delle arance? Sì, ___ compro tre.',translation:'Would you like some oranges? Yes, I’ll buy three of them.',answer:'ne',options:['ne','ci','le'],speak:'Vuoi delle arance? Sì, ne compro tre.',explanation:'Ne replaces an already named quantity of oranges.'}}),portfolio:{title:'Order a quantity',prompt:'Write a short exchange at a ticket office or shop. Name the item once, then use ne with a number.',model:'— Quanti biglietti ti servono?\n— Me ne servono due, per favore.',rubric:['Ne has a clear item antecedent.','The number matches the intended quantity.','The exchange is plausible at the counter.'],'mode':'interact'}});
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-ce-ne-quantity',title:'Say how many are needed',outcome:'I can respond to a quantity question using ce ne.',takeaway:'Ce ne introduces the needed amount when the item is already known; the following verb agrees with the quantity.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-ne-quantity'],words:[['quanti / quante','how many'],['servire','to be needed'],['mancare','to be missing'],['una sedia','chair']],models:[['Refer to known items','After a question about tickets, ce ne avoids repeating biglietti.','Quanti biglietti servono? Ce ne servono due.','How many tickets are needed? Two are needed.'],['Match the verb to the amount','One item takes a singular verb; several take a plural verb.','Ci manca una sedia. Ce ne mancano due.','We are missing one chair. We are missing two of them.']],checks:[['Quanti posti servono? ___ servono tre.','How many places are needed? Three are needed.','Ce ne',['Ce ne','Ci','Le'],'Ce ne replaces the already named plural item.','Answer without repeating posti.'],['Quante sedie mancano? ___ mancano due.','How many chairs are missing? Two are missing.','Ce ne',null,'Ce ne refers back to the chairs.','Use the two-part quantity pronoun.'],['Quanti biglietti servono? ___ serve uno.','How many tickets are needed? One is needed.','Ce ne',['Ce ne','Ne ci','Li'],'Ce ne works with one too; serve agrees with uno.','The item is already known.'],['Quante copie vuoi? ___ voglio quattro.','How many copies do you want? I want four of them.','Ne',null,'With voglio, simple ne replaces copies; ce is not needed here.','Use the quantity pronoun before voglio.']],application:['Check remaining places','Write a two-turn message about seats or tickets: ask how many are needed and reply without repeating the noun.','— Quanti posti ci servono?\n— Ce ne servono tre, ma ne abbiamo solo due.',['The item antecedent is clear.','Ce ne or ne refers to the known quantity correctly.','The number and verb agree.'],'interact','Ask a partner about a different item and amount.']});

// B1.6: make relative reference economical but never ambiguous.
oldLesson('B1','b1-che-cui','v2-b1-che-cui',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-ce-ne-quantity'],facet:'direct-versus-preposition-reference',words:[['il collega / la collega','colleague'],['il libro','book'],['parlare di','to talk about'],['conoscere','to know']],passage:{title:'Finding the right colleague',it:'Cerco la collega che lavora con Marco. È la persona di cui ti parlavo ieri. Ha il documento che ci serve.',en:'I am looking for the colleague who works with Marco. She is the person I was telling you about yesterday. She has the document we need.',mode:'listen',task:'Track the noun that each relative clause describes.'}});
oldLesson('B1','b1-relative-prepositions','v2-b1-relative-prepositions',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-che-cui'],facet:'governed-preposition',words:[['scrivere a','to write to'],['lavorare a','to work on'],['nascere in','to be born in'],['la riunione','meeting']],portfolio:{title:'Introduce a useful contact',prompt:'Describe a person and the project or place connected with them using a preposition plus cui.',model:'Questa è la collega con cui lavoro. Il progetto a cui lavoriamo finirà a ottobre.',rubric:['Each relative clause refers to a clear noun.','The preposition comes from the underlying verb or relationship.','The description helps the listener identify the person or project.']}});
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-clarify-reference',title:'Avoid an unclear reference',outcome:'I can repeat a noun or choose a relative clause so listeners know whom I mean.',takeaway:'A relative clause is useful only when its antecedent is clear; repeat the person or item if two candidates could fit.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-relative-prepositions'],words:[['il responsabile / la responsabile','manager'],['la sorella','sister'],['la collega','colleague'],['consegnare','to hand over']],models:[['Attach che to a clear noun','In La collega che ha chiamato, the colleague is the caller.','La collega che ha chiamato ha lasciato un messaggio.','The colleague who called left a message.'],['Repeat a noun when two people fit','A repeated noun avoids an ambiguous lui or lei.','Ho parlato con Marta e Sara. Marta ha il documento.','I spoke with Marta and Sara. Marta has the document.']],checks:[['Cerco la collega ___ ha lasciato un messaggio.','I am looking for the colleague who left a message.','che',['che','cui','di cui'],'Che identifies the colleague who called.','There is no preposition required by ha lasciato.'],['Questa è la persona ___ ti ho parlato ieri.','This is the person I told you about yesterday.','di cui',null,'Parlare di requires di cui.','Carry the preposition from parlare di.'],['Sono arrivate Marta e Sara. ___ ha il documento, non Sara.','Marta and Sara arrived. Marta has the document, not Sara.','Marta',['Marta','Lei','Loro'],'Repeating Marta prevents an unclear lei.','Choose the explicit name.'],['Ho visto Marco con Paolo. ___ mi ha dato il biglietto: Paolo era già partito.','I saw Marco with Paolo. Marco gave me the ticket: Paolo had already left.','Marco',null,'Marco makes the identity explicit; lui would not resolve the two names.','Use the named person from the context.']],application:['Give clear directions to a person','Write a message identifying which colleague has a document. Use one clear relative clause and repeat a name where two people might be confused.','Ho parlato con Anna e Lucia. Anna è la collega che ha il modulo. Puoi chiederlo a lei.',['The relative clause attaches to an unmistakable noun.','Any later pronoun still has a clear referent.','The reader can act on the message without guessing.']]} );

// B1.7: realistic conditions use indicative forms; hypothetical forms wait for B2.
oldLesson('B1','b1-real-condition','v2-b1-real-condition',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-clarify-reference'],facet:'open-condition',words:[['se piove','if it rains'],['finire presto','to finish early'],['le chiavi','keys'],['chiamami','call me']],passage:{title:'A flexible outing',it:'Se domani piove, prenderemo il treno. Se invece c’è il sole, andremo a piedi. Chiamami quando sai a che ora finisci.',en:'If it rains tomorrow, we will take the train. If it is sunny instead, we will walk. Call me when you know when you finish.',mode:'listen',task:'Identify the two realistic options.'}});
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-plan-options',title:'Offer realistic alternatives',outcome:'I can propose two workable options depending on what happens.',takeaway:'In an open plan, se introduces a possible situation; the other clause explains what you will do.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-real-condition'],words:[['altrimenti','otherwise'],['prenotare','to reserve'],['essere libero','to be free'],['prendere il treno','to take the train']],models:[['State one workable option','A present form after se can refer to a real future possibility.','Se sei libero sabato, andiamo al cinema.','If you are free Saturday, we can go to the cinema.'],['Add the alternative','Altrimenti tells the listener what will happen if the condition fails.','Se non sei libero, ci vediamo domenica.','If you are not free, we will meet Sunday.']],checks:[['Se domani ___ il sole, andiamo al parco.','If it is sunny tomorrow, we will go to the park.','c’è',['c’è','ci sarebbe','ci fosse'],'The open condition uses a present form.','This is a realistic plan, not an unreal wish.'],['Se il treno arriva tardi, ___ un taxi.','If the train arrives late, we will take a taxi.','prenderemo',null,'The future describes the planned response.','Use the noi future of prendere.'],['Se non troviamo un tavolo, ___ a casa.','If we do not find a table, we will eat at home.','mangeremo',['mangeremo','mangiassimo','mangiato'],'The consequence is a real alternative plan.','Choose the future for the response.'],['Se finisci entro le sei, ___ insieme.','If you finish by six, we will leave together.','partiremo',null,'Partiremo states the result of a feasible condition.','Use the noi future of partire.']],application:['Agree on a backup plan','Write a message proposing an outing and a realistic fallback if weather or timing changes.','Se sabato c’è il sole, andiamo al lago. Se piove, prenotiamo un tavolo vicino a casa.',['Both conditions are possible, not unreal.','Each condition has a workable response.','The other person can choose or confirm the plan.']]} );
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-revise-plan',title:'Change a plan politely',outcome:'I can explain a condition and suggest a practical replacement plan.',takeaway:'A condition plus a clear alternative helps solve a real arrangement problem.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-plan-options'],words:[['rimandare','to postpone'],['l’appuntamento','appointment'],['essere in ritardo','to be late'],['invece','instead']],models:[['State the issue without blame','Explain the condition that might disrupt the arrangement.','Se il treno è in ritardo, non arrivo per le otto.','If the train is late, I will not arrive by eight.'],['Offer a replacement','An alternative time lets the other person respond.','In quel caso, possiamo vederci alle nove.','In that case, we can meet at nine.']],checks:[['Se il medico è in ritardo, ___ l’appuntamento di mezz’ora.','If the doctor is late, we will postpone the appointment by half an hour.','rimanderemo',['rimanderemo','rimandassimo','rimandato'],'The response is a practical future plan.','Choose a future action.'],['Se non puoi alle sei, ___ alle sette.','If you cannot make it at six, we will meet at seven.','ci vediamo',null,'A present form naturally states a fixed alternative plan.','Use ci vediamo for a firm arrangement.'],['Se il negozio chiude presto, ___ domani mattina.','If the shop closes early, we will go back tomorrow morning.','torneremo',['torneremo','tornassimo','tornati'],'A real future response follows an open condition.','Choose the future response.'],['Se non trovi il documento, ___ a Marta.','If you cannot find the document, write to Marta.','scrivi',null,'A familiar command can be the response to a real condition.','Use the tu command of scrivere.']],application:['Reply to a changed appointment','Write a short reply explaining what will happen if you are delayed and proposing a definite alternative.','Se il treno è in ritardo, non arrivo alle sei. In quel caso, possiamo vederci alle sette davanti al cinema?',['The possible problem and its consequence are clear.','The alternative is practical and specific.','The tone invites a reply.']]} );

// B1.8: causation, purpose, result and time sequencing in one practical unit.
oldLesson('B1','b1-cause-purpose','v2-b1-cause-purpose',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-revise-plan'],facet:'reason-versus-purpose',words:[['perché','because'],['per','in order to'],['l’esame','exam'],['la febbre','fever']],questions:revisedQuestions('b1-cause-purpose',{3:{translation:'I came (female speaker) in order to help you.',prompt:'A woman is speaking. Put the words in order to express her purpose.'}}),passage:{title:'A cancelled visit',it:'Giulia non è venuta perché aveva la febbre. Mi ha scritto per avvisarmi. Per questo abbiamo rimandato la visita a sabato.',en:'Giulia did not come because she had a fever. She wrote to let me know. For this reason we postponed the visit until Saturday.',mode:'listen',task:'Separate the reason from the purpose of the message.'}});
oldLesson('B1','b1-consequence-concession','v2-b1-consequence-concession',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-cause-purpose'],facet:'result-versus-obstacle',words:[['così ... che','so ... that'],['anche se','even though'],['quindi','therefore'],['la torta','cake']],portfolio:{title:'Explain a surprising result',prompt:'Write a short update with one practical consequence and one fact that contrasts with expectation.',model:'Era così tardi che abbiamo preso un taxi. Anche se pioveva, siamo arrivati in tempo.',rubric:['The result follows logically from its cause.','Anche se introduces a real obstacle or contrast.','The account is understandable as a whole.']}});
oldLesson('B1','b1-before-after','v2-b1-before-after',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-consequence-concession'],facet:'time-and-subject',words:[['prima di','before doing'],['prima che','before someone does'],['dopo che','after'],['la finestra','window']],cards:[...allOld['b1-before-after'].objectives[0].teach,{title:'After an earlier action by the same person',body:'Dopo aver plus a past participle gives a completed earlier action when the subject stays the same.',examples:[{it:'Dopo aver mangiato, siamo usciti.',en:'After eating, we went out.'}]}],portfolio:{title:'Give a short set of instructions',prompt:'Write three steps for leaving home or finishing work using before and after, with clear subjects.',model:'Prima di uscire, chiudo le finestre. Aspetto prima che arrivi Marco. Dopo aver spento le luci, esco.',rubric:['The sequence is unambiguous.','Infinitives share their subject with the main clause.','A finite clause is used where a different subject acts.']}});

// B1.9: present subjunctive forms are supplied before opinions and reactions.
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-subjunctive-bridge',title:'A limited present subjunctive toolkit',outcome:'I can recognize and make frequent present subjunctive forms for opinions and wishes.',takeaway:'After a viewpoint plus che, learn common forms as usable patterns: sia, abbia, venga, possa and regular -i/-a endings.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-before-after'],words:[['pensare che','to think that'],['sperare che','to hope that'],['essere','to be'],['avere','to have']],models:[['Start with frequent irregulars','Essere gives sia, siamo, siate, siano; avere gives abbia, abbiamo, abbiate, abbiano in present subjunctive.','Penso che Sara sia pronta e che abbia tempo.','I think Sara is ready and has time.'],['Build a regular form and learn a few more','Present subjunctive of -are uses -i (parli, ascolti); -ere/-ire uses -a (prenda, parta). Common irregulars include venga and possa.','Spero che tu parli con lei e che lei venga.','I hope you speak with her and that she comes.']],checks:[['Penso che Sara ___ pronta.','I think Sara is ready.','sia',['sia','è','sarà'],'Sia is the present subjunctive of essere.','The form was modelled above.'],['Spero che Marco ___ tempo.','I hope Marco has time.','abbia',null,'Abbia is the common present subjunctive of avere.','Use the modelled form of avere.'],['Penso che Luca ___ domani.','I think Luca is coming tomorrow.','venga',['venga','viene','verrà'],'Venga is the present subjunctive form of venire.','Use the modelled irregular form.'],['È bene che tu ___ con lei.','It is good that you speak with her.','parli',null,'Parli is the tu present subjunctive of parlare.','Regular -are takes -i here.']],application:['Make a cautious suggestion','Write two sentences about a possible plan: one opinion and one hope, using only forms introduced here.','Penso che Marta sia libera domani. Spero che venga con noi.',['The forms after che are from the introduced toolkit.','The subject of each clause is clear.','The opinion and hope have distinct meanings.']],passage:{title:'A possible visit',it:'Penso che Marta sia libera sabato, ma non ne sono sicura. Spero che venga con noi. È bene che tu le scriva oggi.',en:'I think Marta is free Saturday, but I am not sure. I hope she comes with us. It is good that you write to her today.',mode:'listen',task:'Notice which clauses state viewpoints rather than certain facts.'}});
oldLesson('B1','b1-opinion-doubt','v2-b1-opinion-doubt',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-subjunctive-bridge'],facet:'uncertain-viewpoint',words:[['dubito che','I doubt that'],['avere ragione','to be right'],['la risposta','answer'],['sapere','to know']],cards:[...allOld['b1-opinion-doubt'].objectives[0].teach,{title:'More useful irregular forms',body:'Sapere has sappia/sappiano; avere has abbia; venire has venga. These are limited common forms, not a claim that every subjunctive verb has been covered.',examples:[{it:'Dubito che loro sappiano la risposta. Credo che Giulia venga.',en:'I doubt they know the answer. I think Giulia is coming.'}]}]});
oldLesson('B1','b1-wishes-feelings','v2-b1-wishes-feelings',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-opinion-doubt'],facet:'wish-or-reaction',words:[['volere che','to want someone to'],['sperare che','to hope that'],['guarire','to recover'],['mi dispiace che','I am sorry that']],cards:[...allOld['b1-wishes-feelings'].objectives[0].teach,{title:'Useful forms for this situation',body:'Essere has siate for voi; potere has possa; guarire has guarisca for Anna. Learn these exact forms before using them.',examples:[{it:'Spero che Anna guarisca presto e che voi siate puntuali.',en:'I hope Anna gets well soon and that you are on time.'}]}]});
oldLesson('B1','b1-impersonal-judgment','v2-b1-impersonal-judgment',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-wishes-feelings'],facet:'judgment-versus-infinitive',words:[['è necessario che','it is necessary that'],['è possibile che','it is possible that'],['è meglio','it is better'],['partire','to leave']],cards:[...allOld['b1-impersonal-judgment'].objectives[0].teach,{title:'Forms used in these judgments',body:'Partire gives parta/partano; ascoltare gives ascolti; essere gives sia. If no separate subject is named, è meglio plus infinitive is shorter.',examples:[{it:'È importante che tu ascolti. È meglio partire adesso.',en:'It is important that you listen. It is better to leave now.'}]}]});

// B1.10: report another person's message without inventing their view.
oldLesson('B1','b1-reporting-information','v2-b1-reporting-information',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-impersonal-judgment'],facet:'statement-report',words:[['dire che','to say that'],['spiegare che','to explain that'],['partire domani','to leave tomorrow'],['il quartiere','neighborhood']],passage:{title:'A call from Marta',it:'Marta dice che arriverà alle sei. Spiega che prima deve ritirare un pacco. Luca dice che la aspetterà davanti alla stazione.',en:'Marta says she will arrive at six. She explains that first she has to collect a package. Luca says he will wait for her in front of the station.',mode:'listen',task:'Separate Marta’s information from Luca’s response.'}});
oldLesson('B1','b1-indirect-questions','v2-b1-indirect-questions',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-reporting-information'],facet:'embedded-question',words:[['chiedere se','to ask whether'],['non sapere dove','not to know where'],['il biglietto','ticket'],['essere aperto','to be open']],portfolio:{title:'Ask for missing information',prompt:'Write a short message saying what you know and what you still need to ask.',model:'Marta dice che il negozio apre alle nove. Non so se vende anche i biglietti; glielo chiederò.',rubric:['Reported information is attributed to a source.','The embedded question names the missing information.','The reader can see the next practical step.']}});
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-relay-voicemail',title:'Relay a short message',outcome:'I can pass on a short voicemail without changing the facts.',takeaway:'Preserve the source, time and request when relaying a message; do not turn uncertainty into a fact.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-indirect-questions'],words:[['il messaggio vocale','voice message'],['richiamare','to call back'],['alle sei','at six'],['forse','perhaps']],models:[['Attribute the message','Name who said the information.','Sara dice che arriverà alle sei.','Sara says she will arrive at six.'],['Keep uncertainty and requests','Forse remains uncertainty; a request to call back is still a request.','Dice che forse farà tardi e chiede di richiamarla.','She says she may be late and asks to be called back.']],checks:[['Sara: «Arrivo alle sei». Sara dice che ___ alle sei.','Sara: “I arrive at six.” Sara says she is arriving at six.','arriva',['arriva','arrivava','sia arrivata'],'A current statement reported now keeps the present.','Keep Sara as the subject.'],['Luca: «Forse parto domani». Luca dice che ___ domani.','Luca: “Perhaps I leave tomorrow.” Luca says he may leave tomorrow.','forse parte',null,'Forse keeps Luca’s uncertainty in the report.','Do not drop forse.'],['Marta: «Non ho il biglietto». Marta dice che non ___ il biglietto.','Marta: “I do not have the ticket.” Marta says she does not have the ticket.','ha',['ha','abbia','aveva'],'This current report retains the stated present fact.','Report the negative fact, not a doubt about it.'],['Paolo: «Chiamami alle sette». Paolo chiede di ___ alle sette.','Paolo: “Call me at seven.” Paolo asks to be called at seven.','chiamarlo',null,'Chiamarlo preserves Paolo as the person to call.','Use chiamare plus lo.']],application:['Relay a voicemail to a colleague','Listen to or read a short message, then tell a colleague who said what, when, and whether it is certain.','Sara dice che arriverà alle sei, ma forse farà tardi. Chiede di chiamarla se cambia l’orario.',['The original speaker is named.','Time, negation and uncertainty are preserved.','The requested action is accurate.'],'mediate'],passage:{title:'The voicemail',it:'Ciao, sono Sara. Arrivo alle sei, ma forse il treno farà tardi. Se cambia l’orario, chiamami sul cellulare. Grazie.',en:'Hi, it’s Sara. I arrive at six, but the train may be late. If the time changes, call me on my mobile. Thanks.',mode:'listen',task:'Relay the time, uncertainty and request accurately.'}});

// B1.11: general rules and a simple passive for notices.
oldLesson('B1','b1-impersonal-si','v2-b1-impersonal-si',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-relay-voicemail'],facet:'general-actor',words:[['in biblioteca','in the library'],['ad alta voce','aloud'],['si vive bene','people live well'],['si è stanchi','one is tired']],passage:{title:'Library notice',it:'In biblioteca si parla a bassa voce. Non si mangia nelle sale. I libri si restituiscono entro due settimane.',en:'In the library people speak quietly. Eating is not allowed in the rooms. Books are returned within two weeks.',mode:'listen',task:'Identify the general rules and the rule about books.'}});
oldLesson('B1','b1-passive-present','v2-b1-passive-present',{prerequisites:['v2-b1-impersonal-si'],facet:'focus-on-receiver',words:[['il museo','museum'],['la porta','door'],['le pizze','pizzas'],['firmare','to sign']],portfolio:{title:'Write a clear notice',prompt:'Write two short service notices: one general rule and one passive statement about a thing.',model:'Qui non si fuma. I documenti vengono controllati all’ingresso.',rubric:['The general rule does not invent a specific actor.','The passive foregrounds the thing affected.','Agreement matches the singular or plural subject.']}});
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-read-rules',title:'Read and answer a rule',outcome:'I can extract the action required by a short public notice and reply clearly.',takeaway:'A notice may use impersonal si or passive; tell the reader what action matters in plain language.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-passive-present'],words:[['l’ingresso','entrance'],['il documento','document'],['mostrare','to show'],['vietato','forbidden']],models:[['Notice a general prohibition','Non si entra means people may not enter.','Qui non si entra dopo le otto.','No one may enter here after eight.'],['Notice what happens to an item','The passive can state what must happen to the document.','I documenti vengono controllati all’ingresso.','Documents are checked at the entrance.']],checks:[['Qui non ___ dopo le otto.','No one may enter here after eight.','si entra',['si entra','entrano','è entrato'],'Si entra expresses a general rule.','Use impersonal si.'],['I documenti ___ controllati all’ingresso.','Documents are checked at the entrance.','vengono',null,'The plural documents take vengono in the passive.','Match the plural subject.'],['Nel museo non ___ fotografie.','People do not take photographs in the museum.','si fanno',['si fanno','si fa','fanno'],'With fotografie as plural subject, si fanno is the sign’s natural form.','The sign refers to plural photographs.'],['Il biglietto ___ mostrato prima di entrare.','The ticket is shown before entering.','viene',null,'Il biglietto is singular, so the passive auxiliary is viene.','Match the singular thing.']],application:['Explain a museum notice','Read the notice and tell a visitor in simple Italian what to do before entering and what is prohibited.','Prima di entrare, mostra il biglietto all’ingresso. Nel museo non si fanno fotografie.',['Both practical actions are accurately preserved.','The explanation is easier to act on than the notice alone.','Negation and location are not lost.'],'mediate'],passage:{title:'At the entrance',it:'Il biglietto viene controllato all’ingresso. Nel museo non si fanno fotografie. Gli zaini si lasciano al guardaroba.',en:'The ticket is checked at the entrance. Photographs are not taken in the museum. Backpacks are left at the cloakroom.',mode:'read',task:'Find the ticket, photo and backpack rules.'}});

// B1.12: integrate familiar situations without treating an open task as auto-graded.
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-capstone-account',title:'Explain a delayed arrival',outcome:'I can give a coherent account of a delay, prior cause and outcome.',takeaway:'A useful account distinguishes background, earlier cause and the action taken next.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-read-rules'],words:[['il ritardo','delay'],['il treno','train'],['avvisare','to let someone know'],['il binario','platform']],models:[['Set the past scene','The listener needs to know what was happening.','Aspettavo il treno quando ho sentito l’annuncio.','I was waiting for the train when I heard the announcement.'],['Explain the earlier cause and response','Trapassato gives what had happened before; then say what you did.','Il treno era già partito. Per questo ho chiamato Marta.','The train had already left. For this reason I called Marta.']],checks:[['Aspettavo sul binario quando ___ l’annuncio.','I was waiting on the platform when I heard the announcement.','ho sentito',['ho sentito','sentivo','sentirò'],'The announcement is the bounded event.','Which form moves the story forward?'],['Quando sono arrivato, il treno ___ già partito.','When I arrived, the train had already left.','era',null,'The departure preceded my arrival.','Use trapassato with partire.'],['Il treno era partito; ___ ho chiamato Marta.','The train had left; for this reason I called Marta.','per questo',['per questo','anche se','mentre'],'The phone call was the response to the missed train.','Choose the consequence link.'],['Marta: «Aspettami al bar». Marta mi chiede di ___ al bar.','Marta: “Wait for me at the café.” Marta asks me to wait for her at the café.','aspettarla',null,'The object pronoun refers to Marta.','Preserve whom I am to wait for.']],application:['Send the full explanation','Record or write a 45-second account to someone waiting for you: explain the scene, earlier cause, outcome and new plan.','Aspettavo sul binario quando ho sentito l’annuncio. Il treno era già partito. Per questo ho chiamato Marta e abbiamo deciso di incontrarci al bar.',['The listener can follow the timeline.','The earlier cause and practical response are explicit.','The new plan is actionable.'],'speak'],passage:{title:'A late message',it:'Ciao Marta. Sono arrivato sul binario alle otto, ma il treno era già partito. Aspettavo informazioni quando hanno annunciato il prossimo treno. Ti richiamo appena so l’orario.',en:'Hi Marta. I arrived on the platform at eight, but the train had already left. I was waiting for information when they announced the next train. I’ll call you back as soon as I know the time.',mode:'listen',task:'Identify the earlier event and the promise about the next call.'}});
fresh('B1',{id:'v2-b1-capstone-service',title:'Resolve a service problem',outcome:'I can state a problem, ask a specific question and propose a workable response.',takeaway:'In a service exchange, name the item, ask for the needed information and give a realistic fallback.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-capstone-account'],words:[['la prenotazione','reservation'],['il modulo','form'],['lo sportello','service desk'],['disponibile','available']],models:[['State the problem precisely','Give the staff member the key fact and the missing item.','Ho una prenotazione, ma non trovo il modulo.','I have a reservation, but I cannot find the form.'],['Ask for a solution','Use an embedded question and, if useful, an open condition.','Sa se posso ritirarlo qui? Se non è disponibile, torno domani.','Do you know if I can collect it here? If it is unavailable, I will return tomorrow.']],checks:[['Non so ___ lo sportello è ancora aperto.','I do not know whether the service desk is still open.','se',['se','che','cui'],'Se introduces the embedded yes/no question.','Ask whether it is open.'],['Il modulo? ___ può dare, per favore?','The form? Can you give it to me, please?','Me lo',null,'Me lo refers to the form for me.','Keep both recipient and item.'],['Se oggi non è disponibile, ___ domani.','If it is not available today, I will return tomorrow.','tornerò',['tornerò','tornassi','tornato'],'The response is a realistic future plan.','Use a future response.'],['Sa ___ posso ritirare il documento?','Do you know where I can collect the document?','dove',null,'Dove asks for the location.','The needed information is a place.']],application:['Role-play at a service desk','With a partner, ask for a missing form, ask when or where it is available, and give a backup plan.','— Ho una prenotazione, ma non trovo il modulo. Me lo può dare?\n— Oggi non è disponibile.\n— Sa se posso ritirarlo domani?',['The problem and request are specific.','Pronouns refer to a clear item.','A possible next step is agreed.'],'interact','The partner should respond with a new opening time or location.']});
fresh('B1',{
  id:'v2-b1-capstone-relay',title:'Pass on practical information',
  outcome:'I can extract and summarize a substantial notice for someone who needs to act.',
  takeaway:'A useful relay preserves the source, exact time, condition and required action; reading checks remain separate from open mediation.',
  prerequisites:['v2-b1-capstone-service'],
  words:[['il biglietto nominativo','ticket with a name on it'],['l’ingresso','entrance'],['il giardino','garden'],['rimandare','to postpone'],['la conferma','confirmation']],
  models:[
    ['Find two times without confusing them','A notice may give both opening time and event time. Read which action each time belongs to.','La stazione apre alle sette; il treno parte alle otto.','The station opens at seven; the train leaves at eight.'],
    ['Keep a condition attached to its action','A condition can change one activity while another continues.','Se piove, il mercato si sposta sotto i portici; i negozi restano aperti.','If it rains, the market moves under the arcades; the shops stay open.']
  ],
  checks:[
    ['Secondo l’avviso, la visita guidata inizia alle ___.','','nove e trenta',['nove e trenta','nove','dieci'],'The guided visit starts at 9:30; opening time is a different detail.','Distinguish the museum opening from tour start.'],
    ['Il biglietto nominativo viene controllato all’___.','','ingresso',null,'The entry check happens at the entrance.','Find the location in the museum notice.'],
    ['Se piove, la visita del giardino viene ___.','','rimandata a domenica',['rimandata a domenica','annullata senza alternativa','spostata alle dieci'],'The garden visit moves to Sunday; the galleries remain open.','Preserve the conditional change exactly.'],
    ['La conferma alla guida va inviata entro ___ alle diciotto.','','giovedì',null,'The notice gives Thursday at 18:00 as the deadline.','Find the day attached to the deadline.']
  ],
  application:['Send a useful summary','Write a 60–80 word message to a friend: give the start and ticket rule, explain what rain changes, and say when and how to confirm.','Il Museo Civico apre alle nove, ma la visita guidata inizia alle nove e trenta. Porta il biglietto nominativo: lo controllano all’ingresso. Se piove, soltanto la visita del giardino passa a domenica; le gallerie restano aperte. Marta chiede una conferma entro giovedì alle diciotto, per email. Se non puoi venire, avvisala.',['Start and opening times are not confused.','The ticket rule and Thursday deadline are exact.','Rain affects only the garden visit.','The friend knows what to do next.'],'mediate'],
  passage:{title:'Museum and guide notices',it:'Museo Civico — Sabato il museo apre alle nove. La visita guidata comincia alle nove e trenta davanti all’ingresso principale e dura circa un’ora. I biglietti nominativi vengono controllati all’ingresso; chi ha prenotato online deve mostrare il biglietto sul telefono o stampato. Nelle gallerie si possono fare fotografie senza flash. Se piove, soltanto la visita del giardino viene rimandata a domenica; le gallerie interne restano aperte sabato.\nGuida Marta — Per favore, confermate la vostra presenza per email entro giovedì alle diciotto. Se non potete venire, avvisatemi: potrò offrire il posto a un’altra persona. Vi risponderò venerdì con il punto d’incontro definitivo. Il messaggio non dice nulla su eventuali rimborsi.',en:'Civic Museum — On Saturday the museum opens at nine. The guided tour begins at 9:30 in front of the main entrance and lasts about an hour. Named tickets are checked at the entrance; online bookers must show the ticket on a phone or in print. Photographs without flash are allowed in the galleries. If it rains, only the garden tour is postponed to Sunday; the indoor galleries remain open Saturday.\nGuide Marta — Please confirm attendance by email by Thursday at six in the evening. If you cannot come, let me know so I can offer the place to someone else. I will reply Friday with the final meeting point. The message says nothing about refunds.',mode:'read',task:'Find the exact times, entry rule, rain condition and requested reply.'},
  modality:'reading',passageBeforeGuided:true
});

listeningLesson('B1',{
 id:'v2-b1-listen-practical-update',title:'Hear and relay a changed arrangement',outcome:'I can hear a practical change in a short message and pass on the exact detail.',takeaway:'Listen for what changed and preserve the new time, place or condition in the relay.',prerequisites:['v2-b1-capstone-account'],
 words:[['spostare','to move'],['invece di','instead of'],['il binario','platform'],['confermare','to confirm']],
 models:[['Listen for old and new','The new arrangement usually follows non più or invece di.','La visita non è più alle otto: comincia alle nove.','The visit is no longer at eight: it begins at nine.'],['Relay the usable detail','A useful relay says the new detail and, when needed, the condition.','Se piove, ci vediamo in biblioteca.','If it rains, we will meet at the library.']],
 clips:[
  {title:'Changed appointment',it:'Ciao, sono Marta. L’appuntamento dal medico non è più alle nove: è stato spostato alle dieci. Ci vediamo davanti all’ingresso.',en:'Hi, this is Marta. The doctor’s appointment is no longer at nine: it has moved to ten. See you at the entrance.',context:'Il nuovo appuntamento è alle ___.',answer:'dieci',options:['dieci','nove','undici'],explanation:'The message replaces nine with ten.',hint:'Listen after non è più.'},
  {title:'Library hours',it:'Buongiorno. Oggi la biblioteca chiude alle cinque invece che alle sei. Restituite i libri prima della chiusura.',en:'Hello. Today the library closes at five instead of six. Return books before closing.',context:'Oggi la biblioteca chiude alle ___.',answer:'cinque',explanation:'Five is the new closing time; six was the former one.',hint:'Listen for invece che.'},
  {title:'Train platform',it:'Il treno per Como partirà dal binario quattro, non dal binario due. Controllate il tabellone prima di salire.',en:'The train to Como will leave from platform four, not platform two. Check the board before boarding.',context:'Il treno per Como parte dal binario ___.',answer:'quattro',options:['quattro','due','sei'],explanation:'Four is the new departure platform.',hint:'The correct platform comes before non.'},
  {title:'Museum garden tour',it:'Se domani piove, la visita del giardino sarà rimandata a domenica. Le sale del museo resteranno aperte.',en:'If it rains tomorrow, the garden tour will be postponed to Sunday. The museum rooms will stay open.',context:'Se piove, la visita del giardino è rimandata a ___.',answer:'domenica',explanation:'The garden visit moves to Sunday only if it rains.',hint:'Keep the rain condition attached to the garden visit.'},
  {title:'Workshop reserve',it:'Il laboratorio comincia alle undici, non alle dieci. Portate il biglietto e incontrate la guida all’ingresso.',en:'The workshop begins at eleven, not ten. Bring your ticket and meet the guide at the entrance.',context:'Il laboratorio comincia alle ___.',answer:'undici',options:['undici','dieci','dodici'],explanation:'Eleven is the revised start time.',hint:'Listen for the first time in the correction.'}
 ],
 application:['Relay two updates','Record a 30–45 second message to a friend: relay two of the short updates, including the new detail and any relevant condition.','La biblioteca oggi chiude alle cinque, non alle sei, quindi dobbiamo restituire i libri prima. Se domani piove, la visita del giardino del museo sarà rimandata a domenica; le sale restano aperte.',['Two distinct sources are not merged into one event.','The new time or day is correct.','Any condition stays conditional.'],'mediate']
});
lessons.B1['v2-b1-capstone-service'].prerequisites=['v2-b1-listen-practical-update'];

// Each practical B1 unit also has a connected written input for its response task.
addContextPassage('B1','story-outcome','read','A note after a delay','Ieri ho preso l’autobus per andare al cinema. Dopo dieci minuti il mezzo si è fermato nel traffico. Per questo sono arrivata tardi e ho perso l’inizio del film. Ho scritto a Elena per avvisarla; alla fine ci siamo incontrate davanti all’uscita.','Yesterday I took the bus to the cinema. After ten minutes it stopped in traffic. For this reason I arrived late and missed the start of the film. I wrote Elena to let her know; in the end we met outside the exit.','Read the problem, response and final outcome.');
addContextPassage('B1','earlier-explanation','read','Why the visit failed','Quando Luca è arrivato al museo, la biglietteria era già chiusa. Aveva controllato l’orario del museo, ma non quello della biglietteria. Per questo non ha potuto entrare. Ha spiegato il problema a Sara e hanno deciso di tornare il giorno dopo.','When Luca arrived at the museum, the ticket office had already closed. He had checked the museum hours but not the ticket-office hours. Therefore he could not enter. He explained the problem to Sara and they decided to return the next day.','Find the earlier mistake and the later response.');
addContextPassage('B1','changing-duration','read','A new commute','Per quattro anni Elena ha lavorato a Torino e ogni mattina prendeva il tram. L’anno scorso ha cambiato lavoro e si è trasferita vicino a casa dei genitori. Adesso va al lavoro a piedi. Dice che ha più tempo libero, anche se ogni tanto le mancano i vecchi colleghi.','For four years Elena worked in Turin and took the tram every morning. Last year she changed jobs and moved near her parents. Now she walks to work. She says she has more free time, though she sometimes misses her former colleagues.','Contrast bounded duration, old routine and current situation.');
addContextPassage('B1','pronoun-request','read','A document exchange','Marta ha il modulo per la visita. Paolo le ha chiesto di mandarglielo prima di venerdì. Marta non può scannerizzarlo oggi, ma domani glielo invierà per email. Paolo ha già il numero di prenotazione e glielo manderà questa sera. Entrambi sanno a quali documenti si riferiscono.','Marta has the form for the visit. Paolo asked her to send it to him before Friday. Marta cannot scan it today, but she will email it to him tomorrow. Paolo already has the booking number and will send it to her this evening. Both know which documents they mean.','Track each item and recipient before replying.');
addContextPassage('B1','ce-ne-quantity','read','Supplies for a meeting','Per la riunione di domani servono otto sedie. Nell’ufficio ce ne sono solo sei, quindi Marta ne prenderà altre due dalla sala accanto. Servono anche dodici bicchieri: ne abbiamo già dieci. Paolo porterà gli ultimi due insieme all’acqua. Prima di comprare qualcosa, controllano quello che c’è.','Tomorrow’s meeting needs eight chairs. The office has only six, so Marta will take two more from the next room. They also need twelve glasses: they already have ten. Paolo will bring the last two with water. Before buying anything, they check what they have.','Identify the referent and missing amount of each item.');
addContextPassage('B1','clarify-reference','read','Who has the folder?','Ho parlato con Anna e Lucia del documento. Anna, la collega con cui lavoro ogni giorno, ha preparato la prima versione. Lucia ha controllato i numeri. Ora Anna tiene la cartella e Lucia può rispondere alle domande sui costi. Se devi modificare il testo, chiedi ad Anna; per le cifre, chiedi a Lucia.','I spoke with Anna and Lucia about the document. Anna, the colleague I work with every day, prepared the first version. Lucia checked the figures. Anna now has the folder and Lucia can answer questions about costs. If you need to change the text, ask Anna; for figures, ask Lucia.','Use the explicit names to avoid confusing the two colleagues.');
addContextPassage('B1','revise-plan','read','Two ways to meet','Sabato vorremmo andare al lago. Se il tempo è bello, prenderemo il treno delle nove e cammineremo lungo l’acqua. Se invece piove, ci vediamo alle undici al museo vicino alla stazione. Marco deve comprare il biglietto del treno entro venerdì, quindi gli confermeremo il piano domani sera.','We would like to go to the lake Saturday. If the weather is good, we will take the nine o’clock train and walk along the water. If it rains instead, we will meet at eleven at the museum near the station. Marco must buy the train ticket by Friday, so we will confirm the plan to him tomorrow evening.','Read both open alternatives and the confirmation deadline.');
addContextPassage('B1','before-after','read','Closing the office','Prima di uscire dall’ufficio, controlla le finestre e spegni le luci. Aspetta prima che Luca finisca la telefonata, perché deve prendere le chiavi. Dopo che tutti sono usciti, chiudi la porta principale. Se qualcuno ha dimenticato un oggetto, scrivigli prima di andare via.','Before leaving the office, check the windows and turn off the lights. Wait for Luca to finish his call, because he needs to take the keys. After everyone has left, lock the main door. If someone has forgotten an item, write to them before going away.','Notice where the actor stays the same and where it changes.');
addContextPassage('B1','impersonal-judgment','read','Preparing the visit','La guida spera che tutti arrivino in orario. È importante che ciascuno abbia il biglietto, ma è meglio partire da casa con qualche minuto di anticipo. Marta pensa che il museo sia facile da trovare; Luca teme che il traffico sia intenso. Per questo si incontreranno davanti alla stazione.','The guide hopes everyone arrives on time. It is important that each person has a ticket, but it is better to leave home a few minutes early. Marta thinks the museum is easy to find; Luca fears traffic will be heavy. So they will meet in front of the station.','Separate practical advice from hopes and concerns.');
addContextPassage('B1','indirect-questions','read','Questions before departure','Sara dice che il treno parte alle sette, ma non sa se ci sono ancora posti. Marco vuole sapere dove si compra il biglietto e chiede se la biglietteria apre prima delle sei. Marta conosce l’indirizzo della stazione, però non ricorda quale ingresso sia aperto la mattina presto. Scriveranno all’ufficio informazioni.','Sara says the train leaves at seven but does not know whether seats remain. Marco wants to know where to buy a ticket and asks if the ticket office opens before six. Marta knows the station address but does not remember which entrance is open early in the morning. They will write to the information office.','Identify stated information and the questions still unanswered.');

setApplication('B1','past-habits','Contrast then with one occasion','Describe a childhood routine, then a single recent occasion that was different.','Da piccola andavo dai nonni ogni domenica. Il mese scorso sono andata dai nonni una sola volta, perché lavoravo.',['The former routine is marked as repeated.','The recent visit is a single completed occasion.','The contrast is easy to follow.']);
setApplication('B1','ci-place','Suggest returning somewhere','Write a two-sentence invitation to revisit a place already named.','La biblioteca nuova è tranquilla. Ci torno domani pomeriggio; vuoi venire con me?',['The place is introduced before ci.','Ci clearly refers to that place.','The invitation gives a useful time.']);
setApplication('B1','che-cui','Identify a colleague','Write two sentences identifying a colleague by what they do and by something you discussed about them.','Cerco il collega che lavora con Marta. È la persona di cui ti ho parlato ieri.',['Che connects the person to an action without a preposition.','Di cui carries the preposition of parlare di.','The same person stays identifiable.']);
setApplication('B1','real-condition','Plan for uncertain weather','Write a message with two realistic weather conditions and your response to each.','Se sabato piove, restiamo a casa. Se c’è il sole, prendiamo il treno per il lago.',['Both conditions remain open possibilities.','Each has a practical response.','Present or future forms fit a real plan.']);
setApplication('B1','cause-purpose','Explain an errand','Write why you went somewhere and what you went there to do.','Sono andato in farmacia perché avevo la febbre. Ci sono andato per comprare una medicina.',['Perché gives a real cause.','Per plus infinitive gives an intended purpose.','The two ideas are not confused.']);
setApplication('B1','opinion-doubt','Share a tentative plan','Write an uncertain opinion and a doubt about an outing; do not present either as confirmed.','Penso che Marta abbia già il biglietto. Dubito che Luca sappia a che ora parte il treno.',['Each statement is visibly a viewpoint.','The taught subjunctive forms follow the stance.','No unsupported certainty is added.']);
setApplication('B1','wishes-feelings','Write to a recovering friend','Send two warm sentences: one hope for recovery and one personal reaction.','Spero che tu guarisca presto. Sono contenta che tu stia meglio oggi.',['A hope and a feeling are distinguishable.','The person addressed remains consistent.','The form and tone suit a friend.']);
setApplication('B1','impersonal-judgment','Prepare a group visit','Write one necessary action for a group and one simple suggestion without a named second subject.','È importante che tutti abbiano il biglietto. È meglio arrivare dieci minuti prima.',['The named group follows che with a taught form.','The general suggestion uses the infinitive naturally.','Both instructions are useful for the visit.']);
setApplication('B1','reporting-information','Relay a colleague’s update','Quote one short statement from a colleague, then relay it accurately to someone else.','Anna: «Arrivo alle sei». Anna dice che arriva alle sei. Io avviso Luca dell’orario.',['The reported speaker is named.','Person and time are preserved.','The final sentence shows why the relay matters.'],'mediate');
setApplication('B1','impersonal-si','Write two public rules','Write two short rules for a shared space, one permission and one prohibition.','In questa sala si parla a bassa voce. Non si mangia vicino ai computer.',['Both rules apply to people in general.','The prohibition keeps its negation.','The rules are plausible for the same place.']);

// Fresh, skipped-on-first-pass contexts remain available when an independent
