// Written and spoken input recur in every B2 practical unit. These passages
// support transfer and portfolio work; they do not masquerade as graded listening.
addContextPassage('B2','tense-relations','read','An old planning email','Ieri sera Paolo ha scritto a Marta: «Pensavo che tu fossi ancora in ufficio alle otto. Credevo che Anna avesse già preparato la sala e speravo che i colleghi arrivassero stamattina». Oggi Marta risponde che alle otto era già a casa; Anna invece ha preparato la sala solo questa mattina. Il messaggio iniziale mostra ciò che Paolo pensava, non ciò che era vero.','Last night Paolo wrote to Marta: “I thought you were still in the office at eight. I believed Anna had already prepared the room and hoped the colleagues would arrive this morning.” Today Marta replies that at eight she was already home; Anna only prepared the room this morning. The first message shows what Paolo believed, not what was true.','Compare past viewpoints with the later correction.');
addContextPassage('B2','mixed-condition','read','A missed course place','Il corso di fotografia è iniziato ieri. Luca non si è iscritto in tempo e ora non può partecipare. Dice: «Se avessi mandato la domanda la settimana scorsa, oggi sarei nel gruppo». Non afferma di aver davvero mandato la domanda: descrive una possibilità ormai perduta e la sua conseguenza presente. L’organizzatrice gli propone di iscriversi alla lista d’attesa per il prossimo corso.','The photography course started yesterday. Luca did not register in time and cannot take part now. He says: “If I had sent the application last week, I would be in the group today.” He is not claiming he actually sent it; he describes a lost possibility and its present result. The organizer suggests joining the waiting list for the next course.','Separate the unreal past cause, imagined present effect and real next option.');
addContextPassage('B2','reported-commands','read','Meeting notes','Alla riunione, la direttrice ha detto che il nuovo orario entrerà in vigore lunedì. Ha chiesto ai responsabili se avevano già avvisato i clienti e ha detto loro di inviare una mail entro venerdì. Paolo ha risposto che alcuni clienti non hanno un indirizzo email; per questi casi la direttrice ha chiesto di telefonare. Il verbale distingue l’annuncio, la domanda e le due istruzioni.','At the meeting, the director said the new hours would take effect Monday. She asked the managers if they had already notified customers and told them to send an email by Friday. Paolo replied that some customers lack an email address; for those cases the director asked for a phone call. The minutes distinguish the announcement, question and two instructions.','Identify each original speech act and its recipients.');
addContextPassage('B2','agent-and-focus','read','A public decision','Le richieste saranno esaminate entro venerdì. La prima verifica sarà svolta dalla segreteria, mentre la decisione finale verrà presa dal comitato. Le persone interessate riceveranno una risposta lunedì. Il comunicato non indica chi aprirà materialmente le buste, perché quel dettaglio non serve ai lettori; nomina invece gli uffici responsabili delle due fasi principali.','Applications will be examined by Friday. The first check will be carried out by the office, while the final decision will be taken by the committee. Applicants will receive a reply Monday. The announcement does not say who will physically open the envelopes, as that detail is not useful to readers; it names the offices responsible for the two main stages.','Notice when an actor is omitted and when responsibility is named.');
addContextPassage('B2','dislocation','read','A familiar topic returns','I documenti del progetto, li abbiamo già letti. La proposta economica invece non l’abbiamo ancora discussa: Marta vuole controllare i costi prima della riunione. Di questo punto ne parleremo domani con il direttore. La mail usa i nomi all’inizio di ogni passaggio per ricordare al lettore l’argomento; i pronomi riprendono informazioni già note.','We have already read the project documents. The financial proposal, however, we have not yet discussed: Marta wants to check the costs before the meeting. We will talk about that point with the director tomorrow. The email places nouns at the start of each part to remind the reader of the topic; the pronouns resume known information.','Track each resumed topic and object agreement.');
addContextPassage('B2','actor-control','read','Two actors in a report','Dopo aver letto il rapporto, Marta ha telefonato al cliente. Mentre Marta spiegava i risultati, Luca preparava una tabella con i costi. Finita la chiamata, Marta ha controllato la tabella e l’ha inviata al cliente. Se scrivessimo «Preparando la tabella, Marta telefonava», sembrerebbe che Marta preparasse la tabella; il rapporto invece attribuisce quel compito a Luca.','After reading the report, Marta called the client. While Marta explained the results, Luca prepared a cost table. After the call, Marta checked the table and sent it to the client. If we wrote “Preparing the table, Marta was calling,” it would sound as if Marta prepared it; the report assigns that task to Luca.','Identify which actor may be left implicit and which must be named.');
addContextPassage('B2','clarify-intent','read','What the proposal claims','Nel messaggio al gruppo, Anna scrive che un nuovo orario potrebbe ridurre le attese. Marco risponde: «Quindi prometti che nessuno aspetterà più?». Anna chiarisce: «Non ho detto che l’attesa sparirà per tutti. Ho detto che il nuovo orario potrebbe aiutare alcuni utenti. Dovremo misurare il risultato dopo una prova». La precisazione restringe la conclusione senza negare l’intera proposta.','In a message to the group, Anna writes that new hours might reduce waiting. Marco replies: “So you promise nobody will wait anymore?” Anna clarifies: “I did not say waiting would disappear for everyone. I said the new hours might help some users. We will have to measure the result after a trial.” The clarification narrows the conclusion without rejecting the whole proposal.','Compare the original qualified claim with Marco’s stronger reading.');
addContextPassage('B2','reply-remedy','listen','Customer call about the parcel','Buongiorno, chiamo per l’ordine quarantadue. La consegna era prevista per lunedì, ma il pacco è arrivato giovedì. Ho pagato sei euro per la consegna. Non chiedo di restituire il prodotto: funziona bene. Vorrei soltanto sapere se potete rimborsare le spese di consegna e quando riceverò una risposta. Potete richiamarmi domani pomeriggio? Grazie.','Hello, I am calling about order 42. Delivery was planned for Monday, but the parcel arrived Thursday. I paid six euros for delivery. I do not want to return the product: it works well. I just want to know whether you can refund the delivery fee and when I will receive a reply. Can you call me back tomorrow afternoon? Thank you.','Use the caller’s exact request and preferred callback time in your service reply.');
addContextPassage('B2','capstone-discussion','listen','A committee member’s question','Prima di votare, vorrei capire meglio la proposta. Il progetto pilota ha mostrato un calo dell’attesa media, ma riguardava soltanto duecento persone. Che cosa faremo per gli utenti che non possono prenotare online? E come verificheremo se il risparmio previsto diventa reale? Non sono contraria alla prova di sei mesi; chiedo però che il canale telefonico resti aperto e che il comitato riceva dati separati per i diversi gruppi di utenti.','Before voting I would like to understand the proposal better. The pilot showed a drop in average waiting time, but it involved only 200 people. What will we do for users who cannot book online? How will we check whether forecast savings become real? I am not opposed to the six-month trial; I ask that the telephone route remain open and that the committee receive figures by user group.','Respond to the member’s two questions without treating the savings forecast as observed fact.');

setApplication('B2','past-subjunctive','Explain an earlier possibility','Write two present viewpoints about actions that may already have happened, using different auxiliaries.','Penso che Anna abbia già finito il rapporto. Temo che Luca sia partito senza aspettarci.',['Both actions are earlier than the present stance.','Avere and essere are selected appropriately.','The speaker does not claim direct knowledge.']);
setApplication('B2','imperfect-subjunctive','Correct a past expectation','State what you believed or hoped at a past moment, then what actually happened.','Pensavo che Marta fosse ancora in ufficio. In realtà era già tornata a casa.',['The belief is anchored in past time.','Fosse is simultaneous with that viewpoint.','The later correction is distinguished from belief.']);
setApplication('B2','pluperfect-subjunctive','Revisit an earlier assumption','Write what you thought had already happened before a past moment, then what you learned later.','Credevo che Anna fosse già partita quando sono arrivato. Poi ho scoperto che aspettava ancora il treno.',['The assumed action is earlier than the past viewpoint.','The later discovery is presented as a correction.','The timeline is unambiguous.']);
setApplication('B2','past-conditional','Explain an action that did not happen','Write a short message about help you would have offered and the real reason you could not.','Ti avrei aiutato ieri, ma non avevo il tuo numero. Ho chiesto a Marta di avvisarti.',['The offer is unreal past, not a promise for now.','The real obstacle is explicit.','The second sentence gives the actual response.']);
setApplication('B2','reported-past','Retell yesterday’s statement','Present a short original statement from yesterday, then report it from today’s viewpoint.','Ieri Paolo ha detto: «Sono malato e ho perso il treno». Oggi racconto che Paolo era malato e aveva perso il treno.',['Speaker and reporting time are visible.','The completed event shifts to earlier-than-past.','No source fact is added.'],'mediate');
setApplication('B2','reported-questions','Retell two questions','Give two direct questions asked yesterday, then report them without changing who was asked.','Ieri Marta mi ha chiesto: «Hai il biglietto? Dove aspetti?». Oggi racconto che mi ha chiesto se avevo il biglietto e dove aspettavo.',['Both questions remain questions in the report.','The person asked and time viewpoint are preserved.','Se and dove introduce the appropriate content.'],'mediate');
setApplication('B2','passive-tenses','Write a service update across time','Write two notices about a document: one completed step and one planned step.','I documenti sono stati firmati ieri. Le copie saranno inviate ai clienti domani.',['The receiver of each action is foregrounded.','Past and future timing are correct.','Plural agreement matches the documents and copies.']);
setApplication('B2','complex-relatives','Resolve a reference in a report','Write two sentences identifying a group and a document, then say what matters about them.','Ho parlato con le colleghe, le quali conoscono il direttore. Mi hanno mostrato il documento sul quale lavorano; ciò che conta ora è la firma.',['Each relative has a clear antecedent.','The preposition stays with the document relationship.','Ciò che points to a proposition rather than a noun.']);
setApplication('B2','dislocation','Continue a topic-focused email','Write two sentences that bring known items to the front and resume each with the correct pronoun.','La proposta, l’ho già letta. I documenti, li mando al direttore domani.',['The topic nouns are already known or clearly introduced.','Each object pronoun matches gender and number.','The second sentence advances the email.']);
setApplication('B2','infinitive-clauses','Condense a same-actor sequence','Describe how you handled a message: first reading it, then deciding what to do and answering.','Dopo aver letto la mail, ho deciso di chiamare Marta. Le ho risposto dopo la telefonata.',['The shortened actions have the same actor.','Dopo aver locates the reading first.','The final response remains clear.']);
setApplication('B2','gerund-clauses','Explain how one person found something','Write two sentences about a person doing one action while or by doing another; keep the actor the same.','Camminando lungo il fiume, Marta ha visto un annuncio. Leggendolo con attenzione, ha trovato il numero da chiamare.',['Each gerund shares its actor with the main clause.','The sequence is coherent.','No other person is accidentally made the actor.']);
setApplication('B2','argument-links','Make a balanced recommendation','Write a three-sentence recommendation with one benefit, one limitation and a consequence.','Il nuovo servizio costa meno. Tuttavia, non raggiunge tutti i quartieri. Pertanto, propongo di provarlo insieme a un’alternativa per le zone escluse.',['Tuttavia introduces a genuine limitation.','Pertanto follows logically from the two facts.','The recommendation addresses the limitation.']);
setApplication('B2','concession-contrast','Concede an obstacle, then decide','Write two sentences acknowledging a real obstacle to an outing or project, then your decision.','Nonostante la pioggia, siamo andati alla mostra. Benché fossimo stanchi, siamo rimasti fino alla fine.',['Both obstacles are factual in the account.','The two constructions take suitable noun or clause complements.','The decision remains understandable.']);
setApplication('B2','passato-remoto','Annotate a historical episode','Write a brief written account using two common passato remoto events, then one conversational paraphrase.','Nel 1900 la famiglia si trasferì a Torino e aprì un negozio. A voce direi: si è trasferita a Torino e ha aperto un negozio.',['The written account advances through bounded events.','The spoken paraphrase preserves the facts.','The register change is explicit.'],'mediate');

addReserve('B2','subj-regular','È possibile che Sara ___ più tardi.','It is possible Sara leaves later.','parta',['parte','partirà']);
addReserve('B2','subj-irregular','Temo che i ragazzi non ___ il tempo.','I fear the boys do not have time.','abbiano',['hanno','abbia']);
addReserve('B2','fact-or-stance','So che Giulia ___ già a casa.','I know Giulia is already home.','è',['sia','fosse']);
addReserve('B2','past-subjunctive','Penso che Paolo ___ già uscito.','I think Paolo has already gone out.','sia',['è','fosse']);
addReserve('B2','imperfect-subjunctive','Credevamo che i bambini ___ a scuola.','We thought the children were at school.','fossero',['sono','siano']);
addReserve('B2','pluperfect-subjunctive','Pensavo che le colleghe ___ già partite.','I thought the colleagues had already left.','fossero',['siano','erano']);
addReserve('B2','tense-relations','Alle nove temevo che Luca ___ il treno delle otto.','At nine I feared Luca had missed the eight o’clock train.','avesse perso',['perdesse','abbia perso']);
addReserve('B2','unreal-present','Se fossi libero stasera, ___ con voi.','If I were free tonight, I would go out with you.','uscirei',['esco','uscivo']);
addReserve('B2','past-conditional','Avrei voluto aiutarti, ma non ___ potuto arrivare.','I would have liked to help, but I would not have been able to arrive.','sarei',['ero','fossi']);
addReserve('B2','unreal-past','Se avessi avuto il numero, ti ___ chiamato.','If I had had the number, I would have called you.','avrei',['ho','avevo']);
addReserve('B2','mixed-condition','Se avessi dormito, adesso ___ meno stanco.','If I had slept, I would be less tired now.','sarei',['sono','fossi']);
addReserve('B2','reported-past','«Sono in ufficio». Ha detto che ___ in ufficio.','“I am in the office.” She said she was in the office.','era',['è','sia']);
addReserve('B2','reported-questions','«Hai il biglietto?» Mi chiese ___ avevo il biglietto.','“Do you have the ticket?” She asked whether I had it.','se',['che','cui']);
addReserve('B2','reported-commands','«Aspetta fuori». Mi ha detto di ___ fuori.','“Wait outside.” He told me to wait outside.','aspettare',['aspettavo','aspetti']);
addReserve('B2','passive-tenses','Le domande ___ esaminate la settimana prossima.','The applications will be examined next week.','saranno',['sono state','erano']);
addReserve('B2','si-passivante','In questa libreria si ___ anche riviste.','This bookshop also sells magazines.','vendono',['vende','vendiamo']);
addReserve('B2','agent-and-focus','La mostra è stata organizzata ___ comune.','The exhibition was organized by the municipality.','dal',['al','nel']);
addReserve('B2','complex-relatives','Non capisco ___ hai deciso.','I do not understand what you decided.','ciò che',['il quale','di cui']);
addReserve('B2','cleft-focus','___ Anna che ha portato il documento, non Luca.','It is Anna who brought the document, not Luca.','È',['Era','Sono']);
addReserve('B2','dislocation','Le foto, ___ ho già mandate a Sara.','The photos, I have already sent them to Sara.','le',['li','ne']);
addReserve('B2','infinitive-clauses','Dopo ___ la riunione, ho scritto il verbale.','After finishing the meeting, I wrote the minutes.','aver finito',['ho finito','finendo']);
addReserve('B2','gerund-clauses','___ ogni giorno, Marta ha imparato più in fretta.','By practising every day, Marta learned faster.','Studiando',['Studiandola','Studiare']);
addReserve('B2','actor-control','Mentre Sara ___, Luca ha preparato la cena.','While Sara was working, Luca prepared dinner.','lavorava',['lavorando','aver lavorato']);
addReserve('B2','argument-links','Il corso costa meno; ___ richiede più tempo.','The course costs less; however, it takes more time.','tuttavia',['pertanto','inoltre']);
addReserve('B2','evidence-source','Tra dieci e venti minuti hanno aspettato ___ utenti.','','trenta',['venti','cinquanta']);
addReserve('B2','compare-options','Per chi deve arrivare prima delle nove, l’___ è più adatto.','','autobus',['treno','aereo']);
addReserve('B2','concession-contrast','___ il rumore, riuscivamo a parlare.','Despite the noise, we could talk.','Nonostante',['Sebbene','Benché']);
addReserve('B2','respond-objection','Il costo è alto; ___ i risparmi mensili potrebbero compensarlo.','The cost is high; however, monthly savings could offset it.','tuttavia',['perché','inoltre']);
addReserve('B2','clarify-intent','Non dico che sia certo; dico che ___ possibile.','I am not saying it is certain; I am saying it is possible.','è',['sarà sicuramente','era sempre']);
addReserve('B2','complaint-facts','La consegna era prevista martedì; il pacco è arrivato ___.','Delivery was planned for Tuesday; the parcel arrived Friday.','venerdì',['martedì','lunedì']);
addReserve('B2','negotiate-compromise','Accetto martedì, a condizione che mi ___ la fascia oraria.','I accept Tuesday provided you confirm the time window.','confermiate',['confermate','confermavate']);
addReserve('B2','reply-remedy','Il rimborso sarà accreditato ___ lunedì.','The refund will be credited by Monday.','entro',['da','mentre']);
addReserve('B2','passato-remoto','Nel racconto il viaggiatore ___ una lettera e la lesse.','In the story the traveller found a letter and read it.','trovò',['trova','troverà']);
addReserve('B2','remote-pluperfect','Appena ___ chiuso la porta, uscì.','As soon as he had closed the door, he went out.','ebbe',['ha','aveva']);
addReserve('B2','report-versus-story','Nella versione orale: «Lei ___ nella stanza e ha visto la lettera».','In the spoken version: “She entered the room and saw the letter.”','è entrata',['entrò','entrava']);
addReserve('B2','audience-needs','Il laboratorio dura ___.','','un’ora',['due ore','mezz’ora']);
addReserve('B2','source-summary','La segreteria chiede di confermare il numero dei partecipanti entro ___.','','venerdì',['mercoledì','domenica']);
addReserve('B2','capstone-accounts','Nel gruppo pilota, l’attesa media prima del progetto era di ___ minuti.','','venti',['quindici','trenta']);
addReserve('B2','capstone-discussion','Prima di estendere il sistema, i costi reali vanno ___ dopo sei mesi.','Before expanding the system, actual costs must be measured after six months.','misurati',['presunti','ignorati']);
addReserve('B2','capstone-mediation','La nota non annuncia la chiusura dello ___.','','sportello',['sito','telefono']);

// The reported-speech unit precedes the explicit passato-remoto unit. Keep
// reporting verbs in the conversational past so the learner works on the
// shifted viewpoint, rather than having to decode an untaught literary form.
for(const id of ['v2-b2-reported-past','v2-b2-reported-questions']){
  const source=JSON.stringify(lessons.B2[id]);
  lessons.B2[id]=JSON.parse(source
    .replace(/\bDisse\b/g,'Ha detto').replace(/\bdisse\b/g,'ha detto')
    .replace(/\bChiese\b/g,'Ha chiesto').replace(/\bchiese\b/g,'ha chiesto')
    .replace(/Domandò/g,'Ha domandato').replace(/domandò/g,'ha domandato'));
}
{
  const l=lessons.B2['v2-b2-reported-past'],t=l.targets[0];
  l.steps[0].words=phraseWords([['ha detto','said; has said'],['quel giorno','that day'],['aveva perso','had lost'],['già','already']]);
  t.explanation='From a past reporting viewpoint, a simultaneous state commonly takes imperfetto; an action already completed can take trapassato.';
  t.repair.body=t.explanation;
  const card=l.steps.find(s=>s.id.endsWith('.teach-3'));
  Object.assign(card,{title:'Set the reporting viewpoint',body:'Report from the later viewpoint and keep the sequence clear: partiva is simultaneous with the saying; aveva comprato happened earlier.',examples:[{it:'Ieri Marco ha detto che partiva quel giorno e che aveva già comprato il biglietto.',en:'Yesterday Marco said he was leaving that day and had already bought the ticket.'}]});
  const q=l.steps.find(s=>s.id.endsWith('.check-2'));
  q.accepted=['ha perso'];
  q.explanation='Aveva perso makes the earlier loss explicit; ha perso can also be natural when the missing keys remain relevant at reporting time.';
}
{
  const l=lessons.B2['v2-b2-reported-questions'],t=l.targets[0];
  l.steps[0].words=phraseWords([['mi ha chiesto','asked me'],['mi ha domandato','asked me'],['il giorno dopo','the following day'],['se','whether']]);
  t.explanation='A yes/no question becomes a se clause. Keep dove, quando or perché for an information question, and adjust person and time words to the reporting viewpoint.';
  t.repair.body=t.explanation;
  const card=l.steps.find(s=>s.id.endsWith('.teach-3'));
  Object.assign(card,{title:'Shift the time reference',body:'If the question was asked yesterday, domani in the original question can become il giorno dopo in the report.',examples:[{it:'«Vieni domani?» Mi ha chiesto se sarei venuto il giorno dopo.',en:'“Are you coming tomorrow?” She asked whether I would come the next day.'}]});
  const q=l.steps.find(s=>s.id.endsWith('.check-4'));
  q.tokens=['Mi','ha','chiesto','se','avevo','visto','Maria.'];
}
{
  const l=lessons.B2['v2-b2-negotiate-compromise'];
  const q=l.steps.find(s=>s.id.endsWith('.check-2'));
  q.accepted=['è'];
  q.explanation='Both sia and è are natural here: sia follows the modelled cautious formulation, while è states the acknowledged fact directly.';
  q.hint='Acknowledge Friday as unavailable; either the modelled subjunctive or a factual indicative can work.';
}
{
  const l=lessons.B2['v2-b2-clarify-intent'];
  const q=l.steps.find(s=>s.id.endsWith('.check-1'));
  q.prompt='Complete this cautious correction with the present subjunctive.';
  q.options=['sia','fosse','sarà'];
  q.explanation='Sia is the present subjunctive modelled for this cautious rejection; the time cue is present.';
}

finish('B2',[
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-fact-stance','Fact and stance','Build productive present subjunctive patterns and distinguish known facts from viewpoints.',['v2-b2-subj-regular','v2-b2-subj-irregular','v2-b2-fact-or-stance']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-viewpoint-time','Time inside a viewpoint','Relate an event to present or past attitudes by its actual temporal relation.',['v2-b2-past-subjunctive','v2-b2-imperfect-subjunctive','v2-b2-pluperfect-subjunctive','v2-b2-tense-relations']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-alternatives','Real and unreal alternatives','Imagine a different present, then express unreal past outcomes and present consequences.',['v2-b2-unreal-present','v2-b2-past-conditional','v2-b2-unreal-past','v2-b2-mixed-condition']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-report-meeting','Report an interview or meeting','Shift viewpoint, reference words and instructions accurately.',['v2-b2-reported-past','v2-b2-reported-questions','v2-b2-reported-commands']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-institutional-notices','Institutional notices','Control passive time, si agreement and whether an actor matters.',['v2-b2-passive-tenses','v2-b2-si-passivante','v2-b2-agent-and-focus']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-precise-reference','Precise reference','Use explicit relatives, focus and known-topic resumption.',['v2-b2-complex-relatives','v2-b2-cleft-focus','v2-b2-dislocation']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-condense-sequence','Condense a sequence','Shorten same-actor clauses without hiding a changed actor.',['v2-b2-infinitive-clauses','v2-b2-gerund-clauses','v2-b2-actor-control']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-compare-evidence','Compare evidence and options','Attribute a source, compare options and make a reasoned recommendation.',['v2-b2-argument-links','v2-b2-evidence-source','v2-b2-compare-options']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-counterpoint','Respond to a counterpoint','Concede an obstacle, answer it and narrow an overstated claim.',['v2-b2-concession-contrast','v2-b2-respond-objection','v2-b2-clarify-intent']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-correspondence','Negotiate and correspond','Describe a service problem, propose terms and reply with a concrete remedy.',['v2-b2-complaint-facts','v2-b2-negotiate-compromise','v2-b2-reply-remedy']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-narrative-register','Read written history','Recognize written remote past and retell its timeline in conversation.',['v2-b2-passato-remoto','v2-b2-remote-pluperfect','v2-b2-report-versus-story']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-relay-information','Relay useful information','Select audience-relevant details from reading and listening and preserve source conflicts.',['v2-b2-audience-needs','v2-b2-listen-relay','v2-b2-source-summary']),
 makeUnit('B2','v2-b2-integration','Qualified argument checkpoint','Compare accounts, discuss a qualified proposal and brief different audiences.',['v2-b2-capstone-accounts','v2-b2-capstone-discussion','v2-b2-capstone-mediation'])
],[{title:'Council of Europe CEFR Companion Volume',url:'https://rm.coe.int/common-european-framework-of-reference-for-languages-learning-teaching/16809ea0d4'},{title:'Profilo della lingua italiana',url:'https://www.unistrapg.it/profilo_lingua_italiana/site/index.html'}]);

function finish(level,units,sources){
  const pack={version:2,level,title:level==='B1'?'Independent everyday Italian':'Confident and flexible Italian',sources,units};
  fs.writeFileSync(`data/course-v2/${level}.json`,JSON.stringify(pack,null,2)+'\n');
  console.log(`${level}: ${units.length} units, ${units.reduce((n,u)=>n+u.lessons.length,0)} lessons`);
}
